block. \\n\\nIn section 9.2, I'm considering establishing the immutable SceneSnapshot.state, which refers to SceneHead.current_snapshot_id as the logical source of truth, while sidecar records aren't the truth. \\n\\nFor section 10.1, I should define terms like SceneHead, SceneSnapshot, and others, ensuring to include current_version and last_undo info. I also want `GET /scenes/{scene_id}` to return a read model from the head, current snapshot, and sidecars.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Defining data structures and sidecars**\\n\\nI'm considering the potential data structures for SceneHead, SceneSnapshot, and SceneReadModel. For SceneHead, I have properties like scene_id, source, and current_snapshot_id, alongside update timestamps. \\n\\nFor SceneSnapshot, it includes details like snapshot_id and scene_version. I'm thinking about implementing a bookmarks sidecar using `CameraBookmarkRecord[]`, which means I'll remove camera_bookmarks from SceneState. In section 16, I might mention that photoreal galleries will store bookmark snapshots or resolved camera poses. \\n\\nI could also extend the PhotorealEntry to include `scene_version`, `bookmark_id`, and `camera_snapshot` to keep the gallery immutable if the bookmarks change. Additionally, renaming `CameraBookmark` to `CameraBookmarkRecord` would clarify its role as a sidecar.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering CameraBookmark type**\\n\\nI’m thinking about how to approach the `CameraBookmark` type. Instead of removing it completely, I might keep `CameraBookmark` and define it in the sidecar section as records that aren’t versioned. This way, it feels less invasive and still allows for clarity. It’s essential that my design keeps the integrity of the system while making sure these records are well-defined and organized within the sidecar architecture. This seems like a solid compromise!\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating snapshot records**\\n\\nI’m thinking about snapshot records and how they might be recomputed at commit time. They seem tied to snapshots, which are immutable. This leads me to consider that caches could potentially be stored inside the snapshot or perhaps in a sidecar. It's an interesting way to manage data since immutability could provide certain advantages. I really want to ensure my understanding of this concept is clear and accurate!\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering API updates**\\n\\nI'm thinking about adding the `GET /scenes/{scene_id}/versions/{scene_version}` for versioning, which might be useful. However, I'm also cautious not to overcomplicate things since step 2 is about defining rather than implementing. It could be beneficial for retrieving immutable snapshots, but I need to stay within the project's scope. \\n\\nAdditionally, the `POST /scenes/{scene_id}/undo` should create a new head snapshot, restoring the previous editable state with an updated scene response. I might need to maintain concise edits throughout the documentation.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning documentation updates**\\n\\nI'm considering separating the edits for CameraBookmark and Photoreal types. It seems like adding the new 10.6 section before section 11 would help maintain clarity. I'll also need to update sections 7.4, 7.5, 12.3, and 12.4, as well as 16.1, 16.2, and 17 APIs. I might be able to execute multiple small edits through a single edit call with multiple entries. That could streamline the process while ensuring everything is up-to-date.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering update options**\\n\\nI think an update might not be absolutely necessary, but it could be nice to have one. I wonder if I should add a section on snapshot/version and undo semantics, including some bullet points for clarity. I want to make sure this section addresses the key aspects effectively. It's always helpful to provide clear information that others can easily digest! Let's explore what those bullet points could look like.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_qpNKt1kTvZ4Zdl9KcGk4R0XF|fc_0e754b82ab019da10169e1d00539948193b5236e4b6c12803c","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"docs/mvp_duet.md","edits":[{"oldText":"### 9.2 Source of truth\n\nThe only logical source of truth is `Scene.state`, the canonical editable scene state.\n\nThe following may be stored alongside the scene document but are never authoritative and may be regenerated or replaced from `Scene.state`:\n\n* `derived_state_cache`\n* splat assets\n* quick renders\n* photoreal outputs\n* RoomPlan preview meshes\n\n## 10. Canonical scene model\n\n### 10.1 Authoritative state partitions\n\nThe scene document is partitioned into three kinds of data:\n\n* `state`: canonical, user-editable, validator-authoritative scene data. This is the only part that edit plans mutate.\n* `derived_state_cache`: deterministic, recomputable data derived from `state` for UI and validation explainability.\n* output/artifact references: asset pointers, photoreal gallery entries, and splat readiness. These are attached to scene versions but do not redefine room geometry.\n\n```json\nScene {\n  scene_id: string,\n  scene_version: integer,\n  source: \"scanned\",\n  units: \"m\",\n  state: SceneState,\n  derived_state_cache: DerivedState | null,\n  assets: AssetRef[],\n  photoreal_gallery: PhotorealEntry[],\n  last_operation: OperationSummary | null\n}\n```\n\n```json\nSceneState {\n  style_tags: string[],\n  room: Room,\n  camera_bookmarks: CameraBookmark[]\n}\n```\n\n### 10.2 Core entities\n","newText":"### 9.2 Source of truth\n\nThe only logical source of truth for editable scene state is the immutable `SceneSnapshot.state` referenced by `SceneHead.current_snapshot_id`.\n\nThe following may be stored alongside the scene but are never authoritative for editable geometry/material/lock state and may be regenerated or replaced from the current snapshot:\n\n* `derived_state_cache`\n* splat assets and splat job state\n* quick renders\n* photoreal outputs and photoreal job state\n* camera bookmark sidecars\n* RoomPlan preview meshes\n\n## 10. Canonical scene model\n\n### 10.1 Authoritative persistence model\n\nThe persistence model is split into immutable snapshots, a mutable scene head, and non-authoritative sidecars:\n\n* `SceneHead`: the only mutable authoritative record; points to the current snapshot and the single undo base.\n* `SceneSnapshot`: immutable version record containing only editable state plus edit-participating asset bindings.\n* sidecars: bookmarks, photoreal gallery, splat/job metadata, and recomputable caches keyed back to `scene_id` and/or `scene_version`.\n\n```json\nSceneHead {\n  scene_id: string,\n  source: \"scanned\",\n  units: \"m\",\n  current_snapshot_id: string,\n  current_scene_version: integer,\n  undo_base_snapshot_id: string | null,\n  updated_at: timestamp\n}\n```\n\n```json\nSceneSnapshot {\n  snapshot_id: string,\n  scene_id: string,\n  scene_version: integer,\n  based_on_snapshot_id: string | null,\n  mutation_kind: \"initial_ingest\" | \"edit_plan\" | \"undo_restore\",\n  state: SceneState,\n  editing_asset_refs: AssetRef[],\n  last_operation: OperationSummary | null,\n  created_at: timestamp\n}\n```\n\n```json\nScene {\n  head: SceneHead,\n  snapshot: SceneSnapshot,\n  derived_state_cache: DerivedState | null,\n  bookmarks: CameraBookmark[],\n  photoreal_gallery: PhotorealEntry[],\n  splat: SplatAssetRecord | null\n}\n```\n\n```json\nSceneState {\n  style_tags: string[],\n  room: Room\n}\n```\n\n### 10.2 Core entities\n"},{"oldText":"```json\nAssetRef {\n  asset_id: string,\n  kind: \"gltf\" | \"splat\" | \"photoreal\",\n  uri: string,\n  bound_to: string\n}\n```\n\n### 10.3 Supporting types\n","newText":"```json\nAssetRef {\n  asset_id: string,\n  kind: \"gltf\" | \"proxy_gltf\",\n  uri: string,\n  bound_to: string\n}\n```\n\n```json\nSplatAssetRecord {\n  scene_id: string,\n  source_scene_version: integer,\n  status: \"queued\" | \"processing\" | \"ready\" | \"failed\",\n  asset_id: string | null,\n  uri: string | null,\n  updated_at: timestamp\n}\n```\n\n### 10.3 Supporting types\n"},{"oldText":"`CameraBookmark`\n\n* `bookmark_id`\n* `name`\n* `camera_pose`\n* `fov`\n* `created_at`\n\n`PhotorealEntry`\n\n* `entry_id`\n* `asset_id`\n* `scene_version`\n* `bookmark_id`\n* `prompt_modifiers`\n* `created_at`\n\n`DerivedState`\n\n* `zones[]`\n* `clearance_paths[]`\n* `soft_scores`\n* `hard_violations[]`\n* `selection_context_summary`\n","newText":"`CameraBookmark`\n\n* `bookmark_id`\n* `name`\n* `camera_pose`\n* `fov`\n* `created_at`\n* `updated_at`\n* semantics: sidecar record keyed by `scene_id`; bookmark changes do not create a new `SceneSnapshot` or increment `scene_version`.\n\n`PhotorealEntry`\n\n* `entry_id`\n* `asset_id`\n* `scene_version`\n* `scene_snapshot_id`\n* `bookmark_id: string | null`\n* `camera_pose`\n* `fov`\n* `prompt_modifiers`\n* `created_at`\n* semantics: sidecar gallery record keyed to an immutable scene snapshot; it stores resolved camera parameters so later bookmark edits do not alter historical outputs.\n\n`DerivedState`\n\n* `zones[]`\n* `clearance_paths[]`\n* `soft_scores`\n* `hard_violations[]`\n* `selection_context_summary`\n* semantics: recomputable cache derived from `SceneSnapshot.state`, typically stored by `snapshot_id`.\n"},{"oldText":"### 10.5 Model invariants\n\n* IDs are stable across scene versions unless an entity is removed.\n* `scene_version` increments once per committed edit plan that mutates `Scene.state`.\n* `generate_photoreal` and recomputation of `derived_state_cache` do not increment `scene_version`.\n* `derived_state_cache` is recomputed after every committed plan and may be dropped and rebuilt without schema migration.\n* Unsupported captured items may exist as `generic_obstacle` objects. They participate in constraints even if not directly editable.\n* Splat assets are optional and attached by reference only.\n* All geometry uses meters and is expressed either directly in the room-local frame stored on the room or in an explicit `SurfaceFrame` defined relative to that frame.\n\n## 11. Supported object classes\n","newText":"### 10.5 Model invariants\n\n* IDs are stable across scene snapshots unless an entity is removed.\n* `SceneSnapshot` is immutable once committed.\n* `SceneHead.current_scene_version` is monotonic and must equal the `scene_version` of `SceneHead.current_snapshot_id`.\n* Only `SceneSnapshot.state` and `SceneSnapshot.editing_asset_refs` participate in editable version history.\n* `generate_photoreal`, splat jobs, bookmark edits, and recomputation of `derived_state_cache` do not increment `scene_version`.\n* `derived_state_cache` is recomputed from snapshot state and may be dropped and rebuilt without schema migration.\n* Unsupported captured items may exist as `generic_obstacle` objects. They participate in constraints even if not directly editable.\n* Splat assets are optional sidecars and never modify editable scene state.\n* All geometry uses meters and is expressed either directly in the room-local frame stored on the room or in an explicit `SurfaceFrame` defined relative to that frame.\n\n### 10.6 Snapshot, versioning, and undo semantics\n\n* A new `SceneSnapshot` is created only for initial ingest, a successful structural/material/lock edit plan, or a successful `undo_last_change`.\n* Undo never rewinds, decrements, or reuses version numbers. It creates a new head snapshot with `mutation_kind = \"undo_restore\"` whose `state` and `editing_asset_refs` match the prior undoable snapshot.\n* MVP undo depth is exactly one structural/material/lock commit. `SceneHead.undo_base_snapshot_id` points to the snapshot that can be restored by undo.\n* After any successful structural/material/lock commit, `undo_base_snapshot_id` is updated to the pre-commit head snapshot. After a successful undo, the new head snapshot becomes current and the prior undone state is no longer redo-able in MVP.\n* Sidecar records must link back to immutable scene versions: photoreal records reference `scene_version` and `scene_snapshot_id`; splat/job records reference the source `scene_version` they were produced from.\n* Camera bookmarks are sidecar metadata. They are not part of undo history and are not versioned scene state.\n\n## 11. Supported object classes\n"},{"oldText":"5. Result is stored in gallery with `scene_version` and `bookmark_id`.\n","newText":"5. Result is stored as a photoreal sidecar record with `scene_version`, `scene_snapshot_id`, and the resolved camera parameters.\n"},{"oldText":"2. Backend restores previous committed scene version.\n","newText":"2. Backend creates a new head snapshot whose editable state matches the prior undoable committed snapshot.\n"},{"oldText":"* Exactly one structural/material commit can be undone.\n* `generate_photoreal` is not part of undo history.\n","newText":"* Exactly one structural/material commit can be undone.\n* Undo creates a new head snapshot; it does not decrement or reuse `scene_version`.\n* `generate_photoreal` is not part of undo history.\n"},{"oldText":"`generate_photoreal`\n\n* params: bookmark id or current camera, optional prompt modifiers\n* non-mutating job\n\n`undo_last_change`\n\n* no params\n* restores prior committed scene version\n","newText":"`generate_photoreal`\n\n* params: bookmark id or current camera, optional prompt modifiers\n* non-mutating sidecar job\n\n`undo_last_change`\n\n* no params\n* creates a new head snapshot whose editable state matches the prior undoable committed snapshot\n"},{"oldText":"### 12.4 Transaction rules\n\n* Max 5 operations per user turn\n* Entire plan is simulated before commit\n* Entire plan commits atomically or fails atomically\n* One successful plan increments `scene_version` by 1\n* `last_operation` stores plan summary, not raw user text alone\n","newText":"### 12.4 Transaction rules\n\n* Max 5 operations per user turn\n* Entire plan is simulated before commit\n* Entire plan commits atomically or fails atomically\n* One successful plan that mutates editable state creates a new immutable `SceneSnapshot` and increments `scene_version` by 1\n* `generate_photoreal` and bookmark changes are sidecar-only updates and do not create scene snapshots\n* `last_operation` stores plan summary on the snapshot that became head, not raw user text alone\n"},{"oldText":"### 16.1 Inputs\n\n* current committed scene version\n* selected camera bookmark or current camera\n* high-res quick render\n* depth map\n* edge map\n* prompt string from scene state + modifiers\n\n### 16.2 Outputs\n\n* generated image asset\n* gallery entry linked to `scene_version`\n* provider metadata for debugging\n","newText":"### 16.1 Inputs\n\n* current committed scene version and `scene_snapshot_id`\n* selected camera bookmark or current camera\n* high-res quick render\n* depth map\n* edge map\n* prompt string from scene state + modifiers\n\n### 16.2 Outputs\n\n* generated image asset\n* sidecar gallery entry linked to `scene_version` and `scene_snapshot_id`\n* provider metadata for debugging\n"},{"oldText":"`GET /scenes/{scene_id}`\n\n* returns latest scene JSON\n","newText":"`GET /scenes/{scene_id}`\n\n* returns the current scene read model: head, current snapshot, derived cache, and related sidecars\n"},{"oldText":"`POST /scenes/{scene_id}/undo`\n\n* reverts last committed scene change\n","newText":"`POST /scenes/{scene_id}/undo`\n\n* creates a new head snapshot that restores the last undoable committed editable state\n"}]},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"docs/mvp_duet.md\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"### 9.2 Source of truth\\n\\nThe only logical source of truth is `Scene.state`, the canonical editable scene state.\\n\\nThe following may be stored alongside the scene document but are never authoritative and may be regenerated or replaced from `Scene.state`:\\n\\n* `derived_state_cache`\\n* splat assets\\n* quick renders\\n* photoreal outputs\\n* RoomPlan preview meshes\\n\\n## 10. 